sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as User
  participant C as client-core
  participant IDB as IndexedDB (log + snapshot)
  participant G as Gateway
  participant O as Owner
  Note over C,G: network gone: no close event<br/>(Chromium), so 15 s of<br/>silence drops the socket
  U->>C: edits (many)
  C->>IDB: append each op to the log,<br/>then show it
  C->>IDB: snapshot about once a<br/>second, replacing the log<br/>entries it contains
  Note over C: reload or crash: load =<br/>snapshot + later log entries
  C->>C: reconnect with backoff (0.5<br/>s x 2^n, max 30 s, full<br/>jitter)
  C->>G: ticket (REST) then WebSocket<br/>JOIN {since_version}
  G->>O: JOIN
  O-->>C: JOINED: ops after<br/>since_version (or a snapshot<br/>if far behind),<br/>server_time_ms
  C->>C: merge the catch-up under its<br/>pending ops
  C->>G: resend the whole pending<br/>queue, in order, paced 20/s
  O-->>C: OP_ACK for each (a duplicate<br/>gets its original ACK)
